+        addressed_by: "exp4210 gate-blocked because exp4209.selector_trained was False (the upstream build blocked on a wrong-file label lookup). This attempt is gated on exp4220, which OWNS label construction via the proven load_arc_rows path so selector_trained=true is achievable; the gate therefore actually runs on a built oracle-distinct verifier with a matched control + ARBITER conservative-override arm."
+        retire_if_same_verdict: true
+    prompt: |
+      CONTEXT: THE .391 headline gate. A1 (exp4220) built an oracle-distinct learned ARC verifier
+      (verifier_is_oracle=false) on the now-fixed label path. Now measure whether it BEATS majority vote on
+      a HELD-OUT ARC pool -- the deep, defensible claim the circular execution wins cannot make. ARBITER
+      (arXiv:2605.26172) names the headroom: "wrong-majority failures" -- sampled trajectories cluster into
+      basins and vote picks the LARGEST basin, not the most accurate, so the correct answer is in the pool
+      but loses. AggLM (2509.06870) shows a LEARNED aggregator recovers exactly those. The MATCHED
+      no-verifier control (same candidates/budget) is the de-confound the prior circular wins lacked.
+
